{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794234544,"nonce":"ts+JJIcHkKB17be30oZAqDeBP3M=","title":"jno.np.vector of test-function components on a face has the wrong shape","message":"vec(Ft[0], Ft[1], 0.0 * Ft[2]) with Ft = v.bind(x=xt, y=yt, z=zt) (N1E test function on a boundary face) evaluates to (n_q, 3 * n_dof) instead of (n_q, n_dof, 3), so inner(w, it) with a per-point vector w raises a broadcasting error inside _eval_integrand ('mul got incompatible shapes (3, 3), (3, 18)'). Workaround: build the tangential trace as cross(n, v.vector.cross(n)).","files":null}]}